<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE soyuz21b-vostochny ascent</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-13 (board): T0 2026-11-14T01:16:00Z (Fri Nov 13 5:16 p.m. PST) per the Tommot city administration (Sakha Republic, near the fairing impact zone) '10:16 Yakutsk time', via https://x.com/afec7032/status/2121264240455504290 ; LL2 updated T-0 to 01:16Z (Go). NOT announced by Roscosmos; Spaceflight Now (feed generated 2026-11-12T15:21Z) still lists Wed Nov 18 date-only. utc shifted by +1560 s; ECEF geometry unchanged.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Soyuz-2.1b/Fregat-M Vostochny (MKA Kinosputnik, KOEN et al.) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT ILLUSTRATIVE. Soyuz-2.1b/Fregat-M, Vostochny Site 1S: SSO rideshare MKA Kinosputnik, KOEN (KA MT-LAB), NPO Kaisant cubesats (LL2 bff2fc91-eddd-4dfc-af26-ac0674cfab4d).
T0 2026-11-14T00:50:00Z (Fri Nov 13 4:50 pm PST) = LL2 NET (Go, window to 01:50Z; LL2 update 2026-11-12T16:00Z &#x27;Reverted back to NET November 14&#x27;, via NSF forum). NOT confirmed by Roscosmos (no announcement yet; Zeya district administration says launch 14-24 Nov, heightened-alert regime 12-24 Nov).
Event times: BORROWED from Soyuz-2.1b/Fregat Vostochny flight Meteor-M 2-2 (5 Jul 2019) theoretical timeline https://kosmonavtika.com/lancements/2019/05072019/05072019.html: BVGD booster sep 117.6 s, fairing 225.63 s, Block A (stage 2) sep 287.48 s, Block I (stage 3) cutoff 560.40 s, upper-part separation 563.70 s. TYPICAL, not this flight&#x27;s timeline.
Altitudes: 50 km @ booster sep and 175 km @ stage-2 sep BORROWED from the Soyuz-2-1a/Metop launch sequence (https://www.russianspaceweb.com/soyuz2_metop.html); fairing-sep altitude ASSUMED by linear interpolation (129.5 km); 200 km at Block I cutoff and separation ASSUMED (no published figure; real trajectory is suborbital before Fregat&#x27;s first burn).
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.837 km/s (circular v at 200 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+563.7 s; the real suborbital speed at Block I cutoff is lower. File ends at upper-part separation; Fregat burns and rideshare deploys are NOT modelled (timing, orbit unpublished).
Azimuth 349.46 deg: great-circle bearing from the LL2 pad to the Unakha-Bryanta confluence (54.5272N 127.4858E, OSM/Wikipedia river data) inside the stage drop zone announced by the Zeya district administration (&#x27;area of the Bryanta and Unakha rivers north of Kirovsky&#x27;; https://portamur.ru/news/detail/v-noyabre-s-kosmodroma-vostochnyiy-zapustyat-soyuz-b/). INFERRED, no NOTAM/NAVAREA coordinates found; a ~98 deg SSO would need roughly 340-345 deg azimuth.
Target orbit unpublished (Kinosputnik: circular ~500-800 km per space.skyrocket.de; SSO per LL2) -&gt; nothing in this file depends on it. No 3DOF sim for this launch: no Soyuz vehicle model, no published orbit.
Pad (LL2): 51.884395N 128.333932E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=349.46 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-14T01:16:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
